// Expected: c1u1 at one session and at two (GitHub issue #38).
//
// Two shares of a 2-of-3 sharing travel in the clear, so the attacker
// recomposes secret at the phase-0 barrier and its confidentiality fails. In
// phase 1 Alice leaks secret itself. That leak is a disclosure independent of
// both shares, so the secret stays held when either share is withheld, and the
// split ties both shares to it: u1 at phase 1. Knowledge used to keep only the
// first way it obtained a value, so the later leak left secret recorded as
// recomposed from the two queried shares, and withholding either one dropped
// it: u0. A later disclosure now replaces a derivation as the record of how
// the value is held; narration of earlier steps still reads the first origin.
// unlink_origin_late_absent.vp is the counterweight, and
// unlink_origin_late_send.vp discloses secret on the wire instead.
attacker[passive]

principal Alice[
	generates secret
	share_a, share_b, share_c = THRESHOLD_SPLIT[2](secret)
]

Alice -> Bob: share_a, share_b

principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(share_a, share_b)
]

phase[1]

principal Alice[
	leaks secret
]

queries[
	confidentiality? secret
	unlinkability? share_a, share_b
]
